{% doc %}
won-howto-schema — emit a HowTo JSON-LD node from a "Label : description" step
list (won-dosage's "when to use" timeline), so AI answer engines can read the
usage steps. NOTE: Google deprecated HowTo *rich results* (2023); this is now
primarily for AI/LLM legibility, not a Google visual feature.

Self-emitted by the block (content_for can't expose child settings to the
section — see [[won-schema-engine]]). Honesty guard: emits nothing when disabled,
without a name, or without at least one real step.

@param {boolean} enabled - the block's emit_schema toggle
@param {string} name - the HowTo name (block heading, falls back to product title)
@param {string} separator - cell separator (':' for dosage)
@param steps - array/string of "label<sep>description" lines
@example
{% render 'won-howto-schema', enabled: block.settings.emit_schema, name: s.heading, separator: ':', steps: lines %}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign howto_name = name | strip_html | strip
  if howto_name == blank
    assign howto_name = product.title | default: '' | strip
  endif
  assign items = ''
  assign pos = 0
  if enabled and howto_name != blank
    for line in steps
      assign row = line | strip
      assign parts = row | split: separator
      assign label = parts[0] | strip_html | strip
      assign desc = parts[1] | strip_html | strip
      if label != blank
        if desc == blank
          assign desc = label
        endif
        assign pos = pos | plus: 1
        capture frag
          echo '{"@type":"HowToStep","position":'
          echo pos
          echo ',"name":'
          echo label | json
          echo ',"text":'
          echo desc | json
          echo '}'
        endcapture
        if items != blank
          assign items = items | append: ','
        endif
        assign items = items | append: frag
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}
{%- if items != blank -%}
  {%- capture won_howto_json -%}{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"HowTo","name":{{ howto_name | json }},"step":[{{ items }}]}{%- endcapture -%}
  <script type="application/ld+json">{{ won_howto_json | replace: '</', '<\/' }}</script>
{%- endif -%}
